WEBVTT

00:08.530 --> 00:09.450
Scotch?

00:09.850 --> 00:11.820
Sorry.
It's Bourbon.

00:12.300 --> 00:13.950
You okay?

00:13.950 --> 00:16.750
It's been some time
since they took your id.

00:16.750 --> 00:20.240
I'm surprisingly feeling fine.

00:20.240 --> 00:24.090
Anyway, are you really okay with having
the Noir of the Immortal Nine here?

00:24.450 --> 00:26.070
I am your target, no?

00:26.470 --> 00:28.460
You saved us.

00:28.460 --> 00:31.840
Besides, Jean doesn't order me
to eliminate you.

00:32.299 --> 00:33.520
I see.

00:34.450 --> 00:36.350
There's no turning back.

00:36.840 --> 00:41.630
I've decided to see
through all this for Noid.

00:42.390 --> 00:45.730
But they're waiting for you on Venus, right?

00:46.140 --> 00:48.520
Are you sure you want to
go there nonchalantly?

00:50.410 --> 00:52.740
Who do you think I am?

00:52.740 --> 00:55.960
No way I'm going to Venus
guns blazing without a gun.

00:55.960 --> 00:57.600
We have a report.

00:58.010 --> 00:59.660
Lady Cyan has disappeared.

00:59.660 --> 01:00.830
Huh?

01:01.390 --> 01:03.840
We took our eyes off for a second,
and she escaped,

01:03.840 --> 01:05.480
with her current whereabouts unknown.

01:05.480 --> 01:06.960
Please forgive our incompetence.

01:07.260 --> 01:11.700
Hey, that explosive girl might cause trouble
if she runs amok again!

01:11.700 --> 01:12.940
Where did she run off to?

01:12.940 --> 01:14.720
Must be somewhere.

01:14.720 --> 01:18.140
Never mind her,
take a look at this!

01:18.140 --> 01:21.770
With this, I'll have double
the power than Rouge!

01:21.770 --> 01:26.440
You're in for a surprise
with this ultimate weapon we have!

01:26.920 --> 01:27.820
What?

01:29.320 --> 01:34.280
Whaaat?!

01:40.450 --> 01:42.000
Sis!

01:48.710 --> 01:52.010
METALLIC ROUGE

03:13.750 --> 03:15.380
You threw it away?!

03:15.380 --> 03:18.210
You threw away that
Anti-Phaser into the sea?!

03:18.210 --> 03:20.410
It was in the way of concealing my person.

03:20.410 --> 03:22.850
So, what's that Anti-something?

03:23.310 --> 03:26.900
It can analyse the frequency
let out by an active Gladiator,

03:26.900 --> 03:29.110
and then...

03:29.440 --> 03:33.240
In short, it's the phase reversing thing,

03:33.240 --> 03:36.240
when you were going against
each other, or something.

03:36.630 --> 03:38.030
Thanks for the explanation.

03:38.520 --> 03:40.950
But you didn't have to throw it away.

03:41.320 --> 03:43.820
I didn't know it was that important.

03:44.670 --> 03:47.000
What is your goal in coming here?

03:47.370 --> 03:49.260
I want to be with my sister.

03:49.260 --> 03:51.400
Huh?

03:51.400 --> 03:53.590
Was she not like this before?

03:54.080 --> 03:55.720
What are you scheming?

03:55.720 --> 03:56.940
What do you mean?

03:56.940 --> 03:58.920
You weren't like this before, right?

03:58.920 --> 04:01.850
You were trying to kill Rouge.

04:02.890 --> 04:05.730
I was not.

04:06.710 --> 04:09.060
I just wanted to play with Rouge.

04:09.550 --> 04:12.410
Huh? You call that playing?

04:12.760 --> 04:14.070
I heard a voice.

04:15.380 --> 04:17.950
Destroy Metal Rouge.

04:18.300 --> 04:21.410
When I hear that voice,
I feel like I have to do it.

04:21.910 --> 04:23.020
Whose voice?

04:23.450 --> 04:24.790
The one who created you?

04:26.730 --> 04:29.040
It's not my masked father.

04:29.630 --> 04:33.130
So the puppeteer created you.

04:33.480 --> 04:36.800
So her wanting to play with you...

04:36.800 --> 04:38.990
...was her initial drive, I guess?

04:40.340 --> 04:43.780
The voice might actually come back.

04:43.780 --> 04:46.720
Doesn't every Nean hear that voice?

04:46.720 --> 04:48.910
You hear that too sometimes, right?

04:48.910 --> 04:50.190
Nope.

04:50.190 --> 04:53.900
Hang on, you're a Nean?

04:53.900 --> 04:56.360
Oh, you didn't know?

04:56.360 --> 04:57.740
No way!

04:57.740 --> 05:00.400
First is quite a clandestine one, after all.

05:00.400 --> 05:02.410
Don't call me that!

05:02.800 --> 05:04.640
What do you mean First?

05:04.640 --> 05:05.910
Naomi's real name.

05:05.910 --> 05:07.500
It's not!

05:09.660 --> 05:11.340
Back off from Rouge!

05:11.340 --> 05:12.170
No.

05:12.170 --> 05:15.470
We can't afford
to have her here long!

05:15.960 --> 05:17.450
What do we do?

05:18.280 --> 05:21.350
Yeah, let's go with the cold equation.

05:21.350 --> 05:24.760
You want to throw her out to the space?
Now that's cruel.

05:25.070 --> 05:27.830
She's a better Gladiator than Rouge.

05:27.830 --> 05:30.330
We can't contain her
once she runs amok, right?

05:30.330 --> 05:33.100
Better? In which part?

05:33.390 --> 05:35.840
She could tell in an instant
that I am a Nean.

05:35.840 --> 05:39.270
Your insensitivity for not realising it
even though I was always next to you...

05:39.270 --> 05:42.110
...must've been improved for her, am I right?

05:42.440 --> 05:43.910
Beat it, First.

05:43.910 --> 05:46.450
I told you, stop calling me that!

05:46.450 --> 05:48.790
Does this ship have an escape pod?

05:48.790 --> 05:51.790
Then we push her inside with a snap!

05:51.790 --> 05:54.880
Wow, we have a cruel lady here, Miss First.

05:54.880 --> 05:59.050
We can't know
when she will hear the voice again!

05:59.050 --> 05:59.880
But then...

05:59.880 --> 06:00.720
No.

06:02.050 --> 06:04.930
I won't... I won't!

06:04.930 --> 06:06.800
H-Hey...

06:07.070 --> 06:10.760
I don't want to!

06:10.760 --> 06:12.640
- No way!
- That's quite the rebellion.

06:12.640 --> 06:14.820
Stop it!

06:14.820 --> 06:17.170
You're putting us in danger!

06:18.080 --> 06:19.400
Let's play together.

06:19.400 --> 06:20.200
Huh?

06:24.660 --> 06:25.490
Really?

06:25.930 --> 06:26.760
Yeah.

06:26.760 --> 06:27.780
Yay!

06:35.920 --> 06:39.370
Welcome, ladies and gentlemen.
Right this way.

06:43.480 --> 06:46.520
We Altar have secured this area,

06:46.960 --> 06:49.230
and the Neans forced to do labour here...

06:49.230 --> 06:52.020
...have been relocated
to a temporary safe shelter.

06:52.520 --> 06:55.900
You're well aware of what happens
when you disable the Azimov Code,

06:56.470 --> 06:57.690
aren't you?

06:58.010 --> 07:00.800
Revolution.
Freeing the enslaved.

07:00.800 --> 07:03.660
These have already happened
in many occasions in human history.

07:04.500 --> 07:07.320
There are things one can only solve
with extreme measures.

07:10.410 --> 07:12.910
Everyone has arrived.

07:13.730 --> 07:15.500
Thank you for coming so far...

07:15.500 --> 07:20.420
...to attend my humble event.
I truly appreciate it.

07:20.780 --> 07:23.880
It's our event, not yours.

07:24.390 --> 07:26.000
Mister Puppeteer.

07:27.010 --> 07:29.960
I thought you were an Usurper agent,

07:29.960 --> 07:32.010
but it seems like you're human.

07:32.820 --> 07:34.680
Why are you helping them?

07:35.120 --> 07:37.680
I am but a humble entertainer.

07:37.680 --> 07:40.210
The Usurpers are mere sponsors of mine.

07:40.210 --> 07:44.920
They wish to see
the stage set by yours truly.

07:44.920 --> 07:49.240
We possess the same dream
in our chests.

07:49.820 --> 07:53.000
What about you and the Visitors?

07:53.000 --> 07:56.620
Are you able to have mutual thoughts?

07:58.400 --> 08:00.780
Dinner has been prepared.

08:00.780 --> 08:02.940
This way, please.

08:04.570 --> 08:07.010
This is Sis, me, and Dad.

08:07.440 --> 08:10.300
And this is our family home.

08:10.910 --> 08:14.920
Sis and I go to school
from here every day.

08:14.920 --> 08:16.200
That's me?

08:16.200 --> 08:18.350
Your dad's way too mysterious here.

08:19.000 --> 08:21.230
What does he do for a living?

08:23.510 --> 08:24.530
A pancake store owner!

08:24.530 --> 08:25.960
Wow!

08:25.960 --> 08:30.410
This must be one of those learning comics where
you can't judge the profession by their look.

08:30.780 --> 08:34.650
Sis and I would eat Dad's pancakes...

08:34.650 --> 08:38.480
Then we'd dance, and sing,
and play together on holidays.

08:38.480 --> 08:40.480
So it was a horror comic...

08:41.840 --> 08:43.289
Do you like drawing?

08:43.789 --> 08:47.760
I can become anything in my drawings!
It's filled with freedom!

08:48.410 --> 08:49.800
Freedom...

08:49.800 --> 08:53.710
But, calling her your sister
is a bit weird, no?

08:53.710 --> 08:54.360
Huh?

08:54.360 --> 08:57.270
I mean, Professor Eva made Rouge,

08:57.270 --> 09:00.100
and that puppeteer made you, right?

09:00.100 --> 09:02.170
It's not weird.

09:02.170 --> 09:06.070
Dad said Rouge is my sister.

09:06.070 --> 09:08.610
If you were made based on Rouge's data,

09:08.610 --> 09:11.760
strictly speaking,
you're just her copy, eh.

09:11.760 --> 09:13.320
She's my sister!

09:13.320 --> 09:15.340
In other words, a clone!

09:15.340 --> 09:19.430
At the very least,
she's not your sister.

09:20.640 --> 09:22.730
First is the annoying
old lady next door!

09:22.730 --> 09:23.460
Hey!

09:24.960 --> 09:26.050
Sheesh...

09:31.350 --> 09:32.360
What is this place?

09:32.360 --> 09:34.720
Do you like it?
Takes you back, no?

09:35.290 --> 09:39.550
It was meant to replicate
our old house as children.

09:40.950 --> 09:43.440
Is that everyone's ids?

09:43.440 --> 09:47.570
Yes. It would be better
if all the family is here, right?

09:47.960 --> 09:48.720
Family?

09:49.380 --> 09:50.950
But I'm a prisoner.

09:50.950 --> 09:54.640
Soon the Neans will reign supreme.

09:54.640 --> 09:58.290
When that happens,
with you as their Messiah,

09:58.290 --> 10:00.200
you will lead the humans.

10:00.200 --> 10:03.350
Without being able to resist us.

10:03.350 --> 10:05.800
It is a role only you can carry,

10:05.800 --> 10:08.780
since you are part of the family.

10:09.340 --> 10:10.840
You're overselling my ability.

10:11.170 --> 10:15.590
You have what it takes.
I'm pretty sure you're aware of it.

10:16.540 --> 10:18.930
Let's save the complicated matter for later.

10:19.600 --> 10:21.380
Say, do you remember?

10:21.380 --> 10:23.790
Back when we went to the lake together.

10:23.790 --> 10:27.360
That time when Jaron said
he wanted to drive.

10:29.040 --> 10:32.290
That was awful.
I thought I was going to die.

10:32.290 --> 10:34.950
He's been crazy ever since.

10:34.950 --> 10:37.700
I am honoured by your praise.

10:37.700 --> 10:42.660
Eva bought us Broma Chocolates
on the way to the lake, right?

10:42.660 --> 10:46.770
You split one in half
and gave the bigger part to me.

10:46.770 --> 10:49.650
I've been in love with
this chocolate since then.

10:50.620 --> 10:51.960
I don't remember.

10:51.960 --> 10:53.670
Do you remember that moment?

10:53.670 --> 10:57.550
When Jean and I said to Verde
that we wanted to ride a boat,

10:58.100 --> 11:00.610
she said, "No thanks,
my book will get soaked."

11:02.100 --> 11:03.250
That's so Verde.

11:03.250 --> 11:05.310
She was a bookworm.

11:05.760 --> 11:09.520
Achilles was quite a snob
and fashionable one, right?

11:09.520 --> 11:13.650
Yes. She even used an umbrella
even though she didn't need it.

11:15.240 --> 11:17.060
Nius was good at swimming,

11:17.060 --> 11:19.280
and he roamed around
the water like a dolphin.

11:19.690 --> 11:22.800
And to add,
Viola would sing us a song too.

11:23.770 --> 11:26.190
The vacation spent with family...

11:26.920 --> 11:28.650
The best memory ever.

11:30.600 --> 11:33.260
I wish Eden were here too.

11:35.800 --> 11:38.170
Is he still alive?

11:38.840 --> 11:42.390
He's got her id pulled out of him,
so he must be dying a dog's death.

11:42.800 --> 11:45.120
I wonder about that.

11:45.120 --> 11:45.890
Jaron!

11:46.190 --> 11:50.260
Thanks to you using your discretion
to your beloved one,

11:50.260 --> 11:52.270
he's still barely alive.

11:53.060 --> 11:53.820
Stop.

11:54.120 --> 11:59.270
Ah, but, his memories of the loving
family will soon fade away,

11:59.270 --> 12:01.970
and also will the rest of his memories,

12:01.970 --> 12:04.200
then, boom, the end.

12:05.060 --> 12:06.680
I told you to cut it out.

12:06.680 --> 12:08.250
My apologies.

12:09.010 --> 12:12.740
Thanks for the shitty reminiscing talk.

12:14.180 --> 12:14.980
Get in.

12:14.980 --> 12:15.730
Nope.

12:15.730 --> 12:16.750
Get in the bath.

12:16.750 --> 12:18.010
Not a chance.

12:18.010 --> 12:20.610
I am telling you to get yourself clean!

12:20.610 --> 12:22.180
What are you being so stubborn for?!

12:22.570 --> 12:24.580
Rouge isn't coming with me.

12:24.580 --> 12:26.140
I already did this morning.

12:26.500 --> 12:28.200
After being punched by Naomi.

12:29.570 --> 12:31.180
It's just you now.

12:31.180 --> 12:33.840
You won't die just because
you don't shower.

12:33.840 --> 12:35.010
Yes, you will!

12:35.010 --> 12:38.220
If you get some weird virus
and spread it around,

12:38.220 --> 12:40.150
that old man is going to die!

12:40.150 --> 12:40.950
Me?

12:41.280 --> 12:43.950
Humans can die by disease, you know?

12:43.950 --> 12:44.880
You sure about that?

12:46.880 --> 12:48.780
I'm busy right now,
so I'll do it later.

12:49.620 --> 12:52.960
I hereby use my authority as the head
of Department of Divinities to force you!

12:53.820 --> 12:55.750
No way!

12:56.370 --> 12:56.990
Don't run!

12:56.990 --> 12:58.300
Rouge, get her!

12:58.300 --> 12:58.730
What?

12:58.730 --> 13:00.930
Save me, Sis!

13:00.930 --> 13:02.680
Oh, right!

13:02.680 --> 13:05.060
I saw ice cream in the pantry.

13:05.060 --> 13:05.880
What?

13:06.620 --> 13:08.390
That must be a delicacy.

13:08.390 --> 13:13.280
The freezing ice cream would be
the perfect food after bath.

13:13.880 --> 13:14.940
What flavour?

13:15.730 --> 13:18.360
A double stack of vanilla and chocolate.

13:19.050 --> 13:20.500
I'm going in.

13:22.110 --> 13:24.290
I see you're used to handling kids, eh?

13:24.290 --> 13:27.560
I used to be a parent, after all.

13:27.560 --> 13:29.000
So you had a kid?

13:29.000 --> 13:31.370
Haven't seen the kid
since I got divorced.

13:32.690 --> 13:36.580
Whenever I saw Noid,
it reminded me of my son.

13:36.580 --> 13:39.760
So I always tried to not get
involved too deep with him.

13:40.360 --> 13:43.760
I wish I could speak with him more now.

13:44.230 --> 13:47.960
Spending time with him
outside work, doing nothing.

13:49.490 --> 13:51.370
You're only aware they were precious...

13:51.750 --> 13:53.960
...once they're gone.

13:54.710 --> 13:57.190
That might be true.

13:57.530 --> 14:01.650
I also had them...
a family of sorts.

14:02.280 --> 14:04.030
Do you mean the Immortal Nine?

14:04.600 --> 14:06.160
Immortal?

14:07.800 --> 14:10.220
Yeah...

14:10.220 --> 14:13.470
They are also like a family.

14:13.470 --> 14:15.830
But they are a lot more precious
than those people...

14:16.320 --> 14:17.360
Your lover?

14:17.360 --> 14:19.590
For real? Is she a Nean?

14:20.160 --> 14:21.730
My beloved.

14:22.380 --> 14:24.220
That's all there is to it.

14:24.220 --> 14:27.450
If you think of them as a family,

14:27.450 --> 14:29.680
then why are you siding with us?

14:31.320 --> 14:33.330
Regret, I guess?

14:33.330 --> 14:35.760
Just like you.

14:37.260 --> 14:40.060
I'm trying to fulfill
the wish of someone I loved.

14:40.060 --> 14:43.400
That's the least I can do
to make up for my sins.

14:47.910 --> 14:50.910
#10 FAMILY PORTRAIT

14:55.860 --> 14:57.110
Can't sleep?

14:58.160 --> 14:59.420
Nah.

14:59.900 --> 15:03.150
Everyone's talking about family
or that precious someone...

15:03.150 --> 15:05.680
They sure do have memories with them.

15:06.410 --> 15:09.300
Not all memories are pretty.

15:09.790 --> 15:11.640
Well, duh.

15:11.640 --> 15:15.810
But seeing that I can
never obtain such things...

15:16.380 --> 15:18.210
I can't help but feel jealous.

15:21.940 --> 15:24.320
Gosh, I'm on my break, dang it...

15:32.290 --> 15:35.400
If we go in a straight way,
they'll intercept us, and it's game over.

15:35.400 --> 15:39.190
Even if we get lucky and can land on Venus,
we still have problems.

15:39.190 --> 15:40.340
Sis.

15:40.680 --> 15:41.560
Let's play.

15:41.560 --> 15:45.590
Cyan, I'm having a serious discussion
with Rouge now, so hush.

15:45.590 --> 15:48.250
You're the one who should hush.

15:48.250 --> 15:50.930
Stop getting in my way
of me playing with Sis.

15:50.930 --> 15:53.570
Had you not thrown away
that Anti-Phaser,

15:53.570 --> 15:56.000
things would be easier! Got it?!

15:56.000 --> 15:57.100
Now, now...

15:57.390 --> 15:58.590
What should we play?

15:58.590 --> 15:59.730
So we can play?

15:59.730 --> 16:01.730
We'll just go bang and boom like always.

16:02.090 --> 16:04.990
All's well that ends well, as usual.

16:06.650 --> 16:09.160
Rouge, are you really prepared?

16:10.840 --> 16:13.430
This fight is different
from our previous ones.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.480
No room for errors at all.

16:15.480 --> 16:18.250
Don't you want to get Jean back?

16:19.170 --> 16:21.720
That's what we're going to Venus for, right?

16:21.720 --> 16:22.540
No.

16:23.850 --> 16:25.400
That's not all.

16:25.400 --> 16:28.930
I'll stop whatever Sylvia
and the others are trying to do.

16:29.290 --> 16:32.210
I'll protect humanity and Nean freedom.

16:32.950 --> 16:36.180
I'll accomplish
the wishes of my precious ones.

16:36.180 --> 16:38.420
So you're actually prepared.

16:38.840 --> 16:40.960
Then, this is no time for games.

16:41.600 --> 16:42.810
Who's Jean?

16:43.670 --> 16:45.820
Rouge's real family.

16:45.820 --> 16:47.650
Her real brother.

16:47.650 --> 16:48.210
Huh?

16:48.590 --> 16:51.670
Rouge's real brother?
Does that make him...

16:52.240 --> 16:53.960
...my brother as well?

16:53.960 --> 16:55.100
Yeah, yeah.

16:55.440 --> 16:57.670
Just go play with yourself in the corner.

17:00.060 --> 17:01.380
I hate you.

17:01.970 --> 17:03.270
I hate you, Naomi.

17:04.040 --> 17:05.630
I despise you, Naomi!

17:06.260 --> 17:06.880
No!

17:13.550 --> 17:14.579
Naomi...

17:21.589 --> 17:23.190
Oww...

17:23.490 --> 17:27.319
I'll definitely punish her
with the cold equation.

17:28.450 --> 17:31.700
Did you hear someone's voice back there?

17:33.620 --> 17:35.870
Then you're on the wrong here.

17:35.870 --> 17:39.800
Don't just hurt someone
just because you hate them.

17:42.160 --> 17:44.320
Also, even if you hear
someone's voice inside,

17:44.320 --> 17:47.030
it's up to you whether to obey.

17:47.030 --> 17:48.710
You can decide for yourself.

17:49.420 --> 17:50.590
For myself?

17:50.990 --> 17:52.760
Yeah. Can you do that?

17:55.730 --> 17:56.720
I'll try.

17:56.720 --> 17:57.850
All right.

17:58.740 --> 18:01.350
I'll become your true sister.

18:01.770 --> 18:02.570
Can I?

18:04.460 --> 18:07.460
Just like Jean did to me,

18:07.460 --> 18:10.490
I'll become your true sister.

18:14.090 --> 18:15.000
What about Naomi?

18:15.000 --> 18:15.670
Huh?

18:15.670 --> 18:17.920
What's she to you?

18:17.920 --> 18:22.550
You two get along well,
so I'm kind of jealous.

18:22.550 --> 18:23.920
Naomi?

18:24.440 --> 18:26.400
Naomi...

18:28.070 --> 18:30.360
What's her relationship with you?

18:31.610 --> 18:33.570
She's the best stranger?

18:34.130 --> 18:35.440
What do you mean?

18:36.080 --> 18:37.460
Well...

18:37.460 --> 18:40.890
She can be annoying,
but I'm fine sticking with her forever.

18:41.590 --> 18:44.140
Naomi sure is the best stranger
to have around.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.190
What's wrong?

19:12.920 --> 19:13.960
I don't know why...

19:14.600 --> 19:16.720
But I can't remember
the path from here.

19:18.590 --> 19:20.970
Then, let's take it again from the top.

19:23.640 --> 19:24.830
I can't remember.

19:30.040 --> 19:31.180
I remember.

19:31.630 --> 19:34.200
The moment I rode on the boat with you.

19:34.890 --> 19:36.660
It was a fun vacation.

19:36.970 --> 19:41.470
Back then, you looked
like the same age as me.

19:41.470 --> 19:44.160
It felt like I made a friend.
I was so happy.

19:44.780 --> 19:45.700
Me too.

19:46.970 --> 19:50.090
I can't believe you're
taking part in this scheme.

19:50.620 --> 19:52.440
I am against it.

19:52.440 --> 19:56.650
It is Aes the bonehead
with loose screws who's on board with this.

19:57.350 --> 19:58.840
I mean, what choice do we have?

19:59.500 --> 20:01.680
It's so that the Proto Neans can survive.

20:02.290 --> 20:03.970
So that the Proto Neans can survive...

20:04.470 --> 20:06.790
Are you trying to kill me
with that creepy statement?

20:06.790 --> 20:09.890
If we had a different body,
I would've done so with my hands.

20:10.930 --> 20:11.630
Aes.

20:12.370 --> 20:15.490
Do you think this will become
a fun memory someday?

20:25.650 --> 20:26.590
What is that?

20:27.250 --> 20:32.200
Fate will bring the souls to
their most suitable places,

20:32.200 --> 20:35.670
and become the key to unlocking the future.

20:35.670 --> 20:39.870
Is what they obtained freedom?

20:39.870 --> 20:41.510
Or rather...

20:42.320 --> 20:44.850
Is he extracting data from the ids?

20:46.260 --> 20:48.840
The final guests have arrived.

20:50.330 --> 20:50.980
Rouge...

20:52.170 --> 20:57.320
Shortly, our greatest performance will commence.

20:57.320 --> 21:02.950
Ladies and gentlemen,
please enjoy our show till the end!

21:03.400 --> 21:04.990
Multiple flying objects detected...

21:04.990 --> 21:08.050
...at 12 o'clock direction.

21:08.050 --> 21:09.870
Distance, 17,000.

21:10.410 --> 21:11.630
Lock-on confirmed.

21:11.950 --> 21:12.880
Time until contact:

21:13.230 --> 21:19.970
13, 12, 11, 10, 9, 8...
